.TH AENIGMA-VPN-CLIENT 8 "2026-08-12" "aenigma 5.0.0" "Aenigma Administration Scripts"
.SH NAME
aenigma-vpn-client \- configure and start an OpenVPN client connection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aenigma-vpn-client
.B \-c
.I CLIENT_NAME
.B \-d
.I DOMAIN
.B \-p
.I PORT
.br
.B aenigma-vpn-client
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aenigma-vpn-client
installs OpenVPN, if not already present, and configures this host
as an OpenVPN client connecting to a remote server, using
pre-existing client certificate files that must already have been
copied onto the host.
.PP
The script performs the following actions:
.IP \(bu 2
Installs the
.B openvpn
and
.B openvpn-systemd-resolved
packages via
.BR apt-get .
.IP \(bu 2
Verifies that
.IR /etc/openvpn/clients/ CLIENT_NAME
already exists, and exits with an error if it does not; this
directory and its certificate/key files are expected to have been
provisioned separately (e.g. copied from the VPN server) before this
script is run.
.IP \(bu 2
Creates an unprivileged, login-disabled system user
.B openvpn
if it does not already exist.
.IP \(bu 2
Sets ownership of the client's private key
.RI ( CLIENT_NAME .key)
and the shared TLS authentication key
.RI ( ta.key )
to
.B openvpn:openvpn
and restricts their permissions to
.BR 700 .
.IP \(bu 2
Writes an OpenVPN client configuration file to
.IR /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN .conf,
referencing the certificate and key files in the client directory,
and configured to run as the unprivileged
.B openvpn
user/group with TLS authentication and MTU tuning for use over Tor
or similar overlay networks.
.IP \(bu 2
Enables and (re)starts the corresponding
.B openvpn@ DOMAIN
systemd service instance.
.PP
.B aenigma-vpn-client
must be run as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " CLIENT_NAME"
Name identifying the client certificate set, matching the
subdirectory
.I /etc/openvpn/clients/ CLIENT_NAME
that must already contain
.IR ca.crt ,
.IR CLIENT_NAME .crt,
.IR CLIENT_NAME .key,
and
.IR ta.key .
Required.
.TP
.BI \-d " DOMAIN"
Domain name (or address) of the OpenVPN server to connect to, e.g.
.IR example.com .
Also used as the base name of the generated configuration file and
the
.B openvpn@
systemd instance name. Required.
.TP
.BI \-p " PORT"
UDP port on which the remote OpenVPN server is listening, e.g.
.IR 1194 .
Required.
.TP
.B \-h
Display a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The client configuration was written and the
.B openvpn@ DOMAIN
service started successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid or missing arguments, the script was not run as root, or
.I /etc/openvpn/clients/ CLIENT_NAME
does not exist.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/openvpn/clients/ CLIENT_NAME /
Directory expected to already contain the client's certificate and
key material
.RI ( ca.crt ", " CLIENT_NAME .crt, " CLIENT_NAME .key, " ta.key ).
Not created by this script; ownership and permissions of
.I CLIENT_NAME .key
and
.I ta.key
within it are modified.
.TP
.I /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN .conf
Generated OpenVPN client configuration file. Overwritten in full on
each run.
.SH EXAMPLES
Configure and start a VPN client connection to
.I example.com
on port 1194 using the
.I john
certificate set:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo aenigma-vpn-client \-c john \-d example.com \-p 1194
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
This script does not provision, generate, or transfer the client
certificate or key files themselves; it only consumes files already
present under
.IR /etc/openvpn/clients/ CLIENT_NAME .
How those files are securely delivered to the host beforehand
(secure copy, configuration management, manual transfer) is outside
its scope.
.PP
Only
.I CLIENT_NAME .key
and
.I ta.key
have their ownership and permissions modified by this script;
.I ca.crt
and
.I CLIENT_NAME .crt
are left with whatever ownership and permissions they had when
copied onto the host.
.PP
The generated configuration file
.RI ( /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN .conf)
is written using a here-document with variable interpolation
disabled for OpenVPN configuration directives, but is world-readable
by default under the umask in effect when the file is created, since
no explicit
.B chmod
is applied to it; it does, however, only reference key files that
are themselves separately restricted to mode
.BR 700 .
.PP
Each run of
.B aenigma-vpn-client
overwrites
.I /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN .conf
in full and restarts the corresponding
.B openvpn@ DOMAIN
service, interrupting any existing VPN connection under that
service instance.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openvpn (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR aenigma-tor (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Romulus-Emanuel Ruja <romulus.ruja@aenigma.ro>
